ulation) is **[A]** and is the single biggest interpretation risk — the design treats it as bidirectional attention over the time axis and flags that if the source means the latter, C1–C3 must be re-scoped.\n- **Lengths.** T_train = 512 tokens; evaluation grid L ∈ {512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192} = {1×,2×,4×,8×,16×}. Operational definition of \"extremely long\": **L ≥ 16×T_train with (i) no degeneration flag and (ii) error horizon ≥ 8×T_train**. **[D]** — purely my definition.\n- **Sampler.** Identical sampler type and step count (64) for all arms; paired noise draws across arms per test trajectory to reduce variance. Step-count sensitivity 32/128 run on the primary cell only (arms can differ in optimal step count). **[D]**\n\n### Datasets and metric-validity map (each metric used only inside its validity domain) [D]\n| Dataset | Role | Valid metrics | **Invalid / excluded** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **D1a** mixed-OU + fractional-Brownian bank (tunable power-law spectrum, stationary) | mechanism test for C3 | PSD error, structure-function exponents ν₂/ν₄, ACF/integral-timescale error | conservation drift (no invariants); paired per-step error (stochastic) |\n| **D1c** deterministic chaotic multiscale (Lorenz-63/96 cascade, oscillator bank with frequency spread) | primary for the primary endpoint | paired error-growth/horizon, Lyapunov-style divergence, PSD (secondary), DMD eigenvalues | conservation drift unless Hamiltonian variant used |\n| **D2** N-body / spring-mass chain (weakly nonlinear regime) | conservation + long-horizon physics | conservation drift ΔE/Δp, constraint violation, paired error horizon, time-reversal error (reversible variant only) | structure functions (non-stationary) → excluded |\n| **D3** real trajectories (motion-capture joints or video-token tracks) | external validity only | distributional metrics (embedding-Fréchet, MMD, precision/recall, diversity), infill consistency | PSD/structure functions, conservation, paired error, time-reversal → all excluded |\n\nD1a/D1c/D2 give ground truth for consistency; D3 cannot verify dynamics, so it is reported as a transfer check and never used for a causal/mechanistic claim.\n\n## 3. Arms — two tiers\n**Core tier (all run).**\n- **A0** SiT + original time attention, full bidirectional [S-defined arm]\n- **A1** SiT + non-causal Hyena (implicit long conv, FFT, bidirectional mask) [S-defined arm]\n- **A2** A1 with a causal mask on the conv (all else identical) — isolates **causality** [D control]\n- **A3** A0 with sliding-window attention whose window equals A1's kernel support at training length — isolates **receptive-field truncation**, the dominant confound, because the attention arm at long L is otherwise forced to windowing [D control]\n\n**Exploratory tier — declared explicitly: compute-relative, ablation-only, not required for the headline claim** [D]\n- **A4** matched param/FLOP alternative mixers (short conv/TCN; linear attention) — is it \"implicit long conv with gating\" or \"any cheap mixer\"?\n- **A5** no temporal mixer (necessity check)\n- **A6** A1 with kernel truncated to T_train — separates learned long-range inductive bias from kernel support\n- **DL** direct-long training control (§5) and mid-tier size bracket (§8)\n\n**Matching conventions.** Primary comparison holds **trajectory tokens and architecture width/depth** fixed and *reports* actual param counts; Hyena kernel params scale with kernel length (≈18K @1024, ≈147K @8192 for order-2, 6 heads, vs ≈0.59M per attention block), so if |Δparams| > 5% at the operating kernel length, a width-compensated Hyena arm is added to the exploratory tier. FLOP-matched robustness (fewer steps for the long-trained attention arm) is reported as secondary. This is a **[D]** convention choice, not a source requirement.\n\n## 4. Metrics with operational definitions [D]\n**Consistency (needs paired ground truth: D1c, D2).**\n- `ERR(t)` = RMSE vs. ground-truth trajectory given identical initial segment. **τ is baseline