rpretive load**. Primary is unadjusted; secondaries use Holm.\n**Secondaries, pre-ordered:** (S1) arm × log(L/L_train) interaction in a mixed model `LECS, D_PSD_low, ID ~ arm × log L + (1|seed)` — the C2/C3 test; (S2) A1 vs A0 at T_train (C1); (S3) `D_PSD_low`, ν₂/ν₄ (C3); (S4) Fréchet/MMD/coverage/diversity parity; (S5) A1 vs A3 at matched receptive field; (S6) **A1 vs A2**; (S7) DL control; (S8) D3 transfer.\n**Claim gates:** C1 ← S2 non-inferiority; **C2 ← primary AND S1**; C3 ← S3 with gates passed; **C-causal ← S6 must be significant after Holm**; absent S6, the conclusion is downgraded to \"non-causal Hyena performs comparably/extrapolates better\", explicitly *not* attributed to non-causality. Negative control on time-reversed/shuffled-phase data must move the metrics, or the metric set is declared uninformative.\n**Mechanistic readout:** learned Hyena impulse-response support and attention range/entropy in A0, correlated with each arm's β — descriptive only.\n\n## 7. Cost & feasibility (all **analytical estimates**; assumed 20 TFLOP/s effective per GPU **[A]**)\n| Item | Config | Params | Tokens | GPU-h / run | Runs | Est. GPU-h |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A0 attn, A3 win-attn | d384 z12 T512 60k bs64 | 21.5M | 1.97B | 4.3 | 6 (2 arms×3 seeds) | 25.8 |\n| A1 hyena, A2 causal hyena | d384 z12 T512 60k bs64 | 19.8M | 1.97B | 4.0 | 6 | 24.0 |\n| Primary-cell seed top-up (A0@512, A1@8192-eval) | +3 seeds each | — | — | 4.0–4.3 | 6 | ~25 |\n| Eval (2048 samples × 64 steps × 5 lengths) | attn 0.05→2.89 h as L:512→8192; hyena 0.038→0.611 | — | — | — | — | ~30 |\n| **Core total** | | | | | ~24 runs | **≈ 105** |\n| DL control | attn 9.7 / hyena 9.4 (T4096, bs8, token-matched) | 21.5M | 1.97B | 9.4–9.7 | 4 | 38 |\n| Exploratory A4/A5/A6 | d256 z8 T512 30k bs64 | 6.4M | 0.98B | 0.7 | 6 | 4 |\n| Mid-tier transfer bracket | d768 z16 T1024 150k bs32 | ~110M | 4.92B | 53–57 | 2 | 110 |\n| **Grand total (all tiers)** | | | | | | **≈ 257** |\n\n**Halved-budget pruni