, "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"stage": "result", "answer": "# Final experiment design (design-only; **no experiment was run and no outcome is claimed**)\n\n**Provenance legend \u2014 applied throughout:** **[S]** = supported by the source/task text, which grounds exactly two things: an arm \"SiT with original time attention\" and an arm \"SiT with non-causal Hyena operator\". **[D]** = my design choice (arbitrary, sensitivity-tested). **[A]** = assumption (unverifiable; no answer obtainable for `setup_4`/`setup_5`). The phrase \"source says\" is never used outside [S].\n\n## 1. Question decomposition\n- **C1 parity** \u2014 at the training horizon, does the Hyena arm match the time-attention arm on sample quality? **[D]** framing\n- **C2 length** \u2014 does it degrade less as trajectory length grows far beyond the training horizon? **[D]**\n- **C3 multi-timescale** \u2014 does it preserve dynamics across timescales (spectral/autocorrelation/invariant structure), not just one-step marginals? **[D]**\n- **C-causal attribution** \u2014 is any advantage attributable to *non-causality* specifically? Gated, see \u00a76.\n\n## 2. Setup [all D/A]\n- **Model.** SiT-style diffusion/flow transformer over trajectory tokens, d=384, depth 12, ~20M params, MLP ratio 4, per-timestep tokens (or 4-step patches). Only the **temporal mixer** varies; data, tokenizer, interpolant/noise schedule, conditioning, optimizer, LR schedule, EMA, steps and loss are shared. **[D]**; the identity of \"original time attention\" (attention over timestep tokens vs. spatial/agent attention with timestep modulation) is **[A]** and is the largest interpretation risk \u2014 the design assumes temporal bidirectional attention and flags that otherwise C1\u2013C3 must be re-scoped.\n- **Lengths.** T_train = 512; evaluation grid L \u2208 {512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192} = {1\u00d7,2\u00d7,4\u00d7,8\u00d7,16\u00d7}. Operational \"extremely long\": **L \u2265 16\u00d7T_train with no degeneration flag and error horizon \u2265 8\u00d7T_train**. **[D]**\n- **Sampler.** Identical sampler type and step count (64) for all arms; paired noise draws across arms per test trajectory; step-count sensitivity 32/128 on the primary cell only (arms may differ in optimal steps). **[D]**\n\n### Datasets with metric-validity map (metrics used only inside their validity domain) [D]\n| Dataset | Role | Valid metrics | **Excluded** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **D1a** mixed-OU + fractional-Brownian bank (tunable power-law spectrum, stationary) | C3 mechanism test | PSD error, structure-function exponents \u03bd\u2082/\u03bd\u2084, ACF/integral-timescale error | conservation drift (no invariants); paired per-step error (stochastic) |\n| **D1c** deterministic chaotic multiscale (Lorenz-63/96 cascade, frequency-spread oscillator bank) | primary dataset for the primary endpoint | paired error growth/horizon, Lyapunov-style divergence, DMD eigenvalues, PSD (secondary) | conservation drift unless Hamiltonian variant |\n| **D2** N-body / spring-mass chain (weakly nonlinear) | conservation + long horizon | \u0394E/\u0394p drift, constraint violation, paired error horizon, time-reversal error (reversible variant) | structure functions (non-stationary) |\n| **D3** real trajectories (motion-capture joints / video tokens) | external validity only | embedding-Fr\u00e9chet, MMD, precision/recall, diversity, infill consistency | PSD/structure functions, conservation, paired error, time-reversal |\n\nD3 cannot verify dynamics, so it is a transfer check and never supports a mechanistic claim.\n\n## 3. Arms \u2014 two tiers\n**Core tier (all run).**\n- **A0** SiT + original time attention, full bidirectional [S]\n- **A1** SiT + non-causal Hyena (implicit long conv, FFT, no causal mask) [S]\n- **A2** A1 + causal mask, otherwise identical \u2014 isolates **causality** [D]\n- **A3** A0 + sliding-window attention with window = A1's kernel support at training length \u2014 isolates **receptive-field truncation**, the dominant confound since the attention arm at long L is otherwise forced to windowing [D]\n\n**Exploratory tier \u2014 explicitly declared compute-relative, ablation-only, not required for the headline claim [D]:** **A4** matched param/FLOP alternatives (TCN/short conv, linear attention) \u2014 is it \"implicit long conv + gating\" or \"any cheap mixer\"; **A5** no temporal mixer (necessity); **A6** A1 with kernel truncated to T_train (inductive bias vs kernel support); **DL** direct-long control (\u00a75) and mid-tier size bracket (\u00a77).\n\n**Matching conventions.** Primary comparison fixes **trajectory tokens + width/depth** and *reports* actual param counts. Hyena kernel params grow with kernel length (\u224818K @1024, \u2248147K @8192 for order-2, 6 heads, vs \u22480.59M per attention block), so if |\u0394params| > 5% at the operating kernel length a width-compensated Hyena arm joins the exploratory tier. FLOP-matched robustness (fewer steps for the long-trained attention arm) is secondary. **[D]**\n\n## 4. Metrics with operational definitions [D]\n**Consistency (paired ground truth: D1c, D2).** `ERR(t)` = RMSE vs. ground truth from the same initial segment. **\u03c4 is baseline-anchored, not absolute:** \u03c4 := A0's mean endpoint `ERR` at L=T_train. **`H_\u03c4`** = first t with `ERR(t) > \u03c4`; **primary scale-free score `LECS = H_\u03c4/L`** \u2208 (0,1]. `\u03b2` = OLS slope of `log ERR(t)` over the monotone window. **Infill disagreement `ID(L)`** = mean L2 gap in overlap regions when the long trajectory is generated as overlapping windows via masked denoising with shared context (works on stochastic/real data); if masking is unsupported, `ID` is dropped, not proxied. **Conservation drift** \u0394E, \u0394p (D2); **time-reversal error** (reversible variant). **Degeneration gates** (pre-hoc, symmetric): tail/data variance ratio \u2208 [0.8, 1.25]; no >2\u00d7 spectral-entropy collapse; no repeated n-gram segment 