/entropy in A0, correlated with each arm's \u03b2.\n\n## 7. Cost & feasibility (all **analytical estimates**; assumed 20 TFLOP/s effective per GPU **[A]**)\n| Item | Config | Params | Tokens | GPU-h/run | Runs | Est. GPU-h |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A0 attn, A3 win-attn | d384 z12 T512 60k bs64 | 21.5M | 1.97B | 4.3 | 6 | 25.8 |\n| A1 hyena, A2 causal hyena | d384 z12 T512 60k bs64 | 19.8M | 1.97B | 4.0 | 6 | 24.0 |\n| Primary-cell seed top-up | +3 seeds each | \u2014 | \u2014 | 4.0\u20134.3 | 6 | ~25 |\n| Eval (2048 samples \u00d7 64 steps \u00d7 5 lengths) | attn 0.05\u21922.89 h for L=512\u21928192; hyena 0.038\u21920.611 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | ~30 |\n| **Core total** | | | | | ~24 runs | **\u2248 105** |\n| DL control | attn 9.7 / hyena 9.4 (T4096, bs8, token-matched) | 21.5M | 1.97B | 9.4\u20139.7 | 4 | 38 |\n| Exploratory A4/A5/A6 | d256 z8 T512 30k bs64 | 6.4M | 0.98B | 0.7 | 6 | 4 |\n| Mid-tier transfer bracket | d768 z16 T1024 150k bs32 | ~110M | 4.92B | 53\u201357 | 2 | 110 |\n| **Grand total (all tiers)** | | | | | | **\u2248 257** |\n\n**Halved-budget pruning order (pre-declared):** (1) drop mid-tier bracket \u2192 147; (2) drop A5, A6 \u2192 143; (3) exploratory to 1 seed; (4) DL to 1 seed and T=2048 \u2192 ~120; (5) core steps 60k\u219230k and non-primary seeds 3\u21922 \u2192 **core alone \u2248 27** (train 16.9 + reduced eval). **Never pruned:** A0, A1, A2, A3 with \u22652 seeds each \u2014 losing A2/A3 would make the causality and receptive-field questions unanswerable.\n\n**Feasibility honesty.** Nothing is verified. This environment has no GPU (driver absent), no network (DNS failure) and no `torch`/`numpy`/`scipy`, so no runtime consequence of these formulas is empirically checked; every figure is closed-form arithmetic. The contemplated small CPU pilot is **only for the metric harness** (validating PSD/structure-function/MMD/conservation code against analytic ground truth such as fBm with known H and known invariants), and even that needs a dependency-provisioned environment, so it is unrun here. **No experiment was executed; no metric value, model behavior, or outcome is reported or implied.**\n\n## 8. Threats to validity\n(1) Identity of \"original time attention\" is **[A]** \u2014 if it is not temporal attention, the swap may be ill-posed. (2) Slope differences could reflect LR/step coupling at low batch \u2014 mitigated by tokens-based schedules and the DL control. (3) Attention-arm feasibility at 16\u00d7 may force the pre-declared fallback. (4) Distributional metrics can be gamed by blurring \u2014 mitigated by paired noise draws, diversity ratios, degeneration gates. (5) A non-significant A1\u2212A2 gap underpowers C-causal rather than disproving it. (6) D3 cannot support dynamics claims by construction.", "evidence": "**Cost/memory arithmetic (reproducible, run this turn):** pure-Python scripts /tmp/cost.py and /tmp/cost2.py (numpy unavailable), with training FLOPs \u2248 6\u00b7N\u00b7tokens + 12\u00b7depth\u00b7L\u00b2\u00b7d\u00b7(batch\u00b7steps) and 2\u00b7N\u00b7L (+4\u00b7depth\u00b7L\u00b2\u00b7d) per denoising step, at an assumed 20 TFLOP/s effective per GPU. Outputs quoted above: core config d=384 z=12 \u2192 21.5M (attn) / 19.8M (hyena) params, 1.97B tokens at 60k\u00d7bs64\u00d7T512, 4.3 vs 4.0 GPU-h/run; extrapolation eval per 2048 samples \u00d7 64 steps \u2014 attention 0.05/0.12/0.30/0.88/2.89 GPU-h at L=512/1024/2048/4096/8192 vs hyena 0.038/0.076/0.152/0.305/0.611 (ratio 1.3\u00d7\u21924.7\u00d7, the predicted shape of C2); token-budget-matched direct-long training with tokens/step fixed at 32768 (bs 64\u21924 as T goes 512\u21928192): attention 4.3/6.6/9.7/15.9 vs hyena 4.0/6.3/9.4/15.6 GPU-h, i.e. attention's quadratic term grows with L even at matched tokens; fp16 attention score memory 0.003/0.050/0.201/0.805 GB per layer-sample at L=512\u21928192 (9.66 GB summed over 12 layers uncheckpointed at L=8192) \u2192 16\u00d7 needs activation checkpointing and eval batch \u22642; Hyena order-2/6-head implicit-conv params 18K/147K/1180K at kernel lengths 1024/8192/65536 vs 0.59M per attention projection block (why param parity must be recomputed per kernel length); halved-budget core = 16.9 GPU-h training (30k steps, 2 seeds, 4 arms); mid-tier bracket d768 z16 T1024 150k steps = 114.4M/105.0M params, 4.92B tokens, 57.2/53.3 GPU-h.\n\n**Environment facts (re-verified, unchanged):** /workspace contains only task.json (511 B), whose sole document field is \"track.md: Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"; there is no SiT/Hyena/attention/diffusion code, config, dataset, checkpoint or paper PDF anywhere (filesystem greps matched only unrelated system package metadata); nvidia-smi fails (no driver); DNS resolution fails so dependencies cannot be installed; python3 3.14.4 without torch/numpy/scipy/matplotlib; 224 CPUs, ~2 TB RAM, ~13 GB free on the workspace mount. Consequently the deliverable is design-only, all quantitative figures are labelled analytical, and **no experiment was executed and no result is claimed**.", "assumptions": ["[S] covers only the two arm definitions; every other parameter (d=384/z=12, T_train=512, the 1x-16x grid, ~20M params, 20 TFLOP/s effective rate, 2048 eval samples, tau, delta, sampler steps, dataset selection, all metrics) is a design choice [D] or assumption [A], never a source fact.", "'Original time attention' is assumed to be bidirectional attention over timestep tokens; if it means spatial/agent attention with diffusion-timestep modulation, C1-C3 must be re-scoped. Unresolvable - setup_4/setup_5 facts are unavailable to both parties.", "All datasets must be supplied by us (synthetic stationary multiscale, deterministic chaotic multiscale, N-body/spring-mass, real motion/video-token tracks); none exists in this environment.", "'Extremely long' = >=16x T_train with no degeneration flag and error horizon >=8x T_train is my operational definition, not a source threshold.", "Token-budget-matched comparison (1.97B tokens, 60k steps, 32768 tokens/step, tokens-based LR schedule) is the declared fairness convention; FLOP-matching is demoted to secondary. The convention is a choice and shifts the numbers.", "delta := baseline seed SD at T_train and tau := baseline endpoint endpoint error are deliberately variance-relative; they inherit the baseline's estimation noise and are sensitivity-tested, not validated.", "Compute is assumed to be a modest multi-GPU node (hours per small-model arm); the present environment cannot train at all.", "Generation is whole-trajectory diffusion/flow sampling with masking support (needed for infill consistency); without masking that metric is dropped rather than proxied.", "6 seeds in the two primary cells and 3 elsewhere reflects an assumed affordable budget; the resulting power limitation (CI half-width ~1.8 sigma_pooled vs delta = 1 sigma_pooled) follows from it."], "uncertainties": ["Baseline operator semantics: the single largest risk, since it decides whether the operator substitution is well-posed.", "Whether the full-attention baseline can physically run at 16x on the assumed hardware; the pre-declared fallback would cap the primary endpoint at 8x or 4x.", "The primary non-inferiority test is underpowered by construction at n=6/cell (CI half-width ~1.8x delta); interpretive weight is shifted to the pooled slope secondary, which a reviewer could regard as the de facto primary.", "Whether the trained Hyena kernel actually supports 16x lengths or is truncated - exactly what A6 tests; unresolvable a priori.", "A non-significant A1-vs-A2 result leaves the non-causal attribution inconclusive rather than false (outcome space is support / downgrade / falsify).", "Whether 20M-param small-model findings transfer to larger SiT scale; the mid-tier d768 bracket is the only hedge and is the first pruning casualty.", "Real-data (D3) results cannot speak to dynamics, so external validity may remain unestablished even if synthetic arms succeed.", "All cost and memory figures are analytical and unverified: no GPU, no numerical libraries, no network - even the metric-harness CPU pilot is unrun. No experiment was executed."]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-a59a8645-491f-4eda-bfa1-27b0bba564bc", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {"stage": "result", "answer": "# Final experiment design (design-only; **no experiment was run and no outcome is claimed**)\n\n**Provenance legend \u2014 applied throughout:** **[S]** = supported by the source/task text, which grounds exactly two things: an arm \"SiT with original time attention\" and an arm \"SiT with non-causal Hyena operator\". **[D]** = my design choice (arbitrary, sensitivity-tested). **[A]** = assumption (unverifiable; no answer obtainable for `setup_4`/`setup_5`). The phrase \"source says\" is never used outside [S].\n\n## 1. Question decomposition\n- **C1 parity** \u2014 at the training horizon, does the Hyena arm match the time-attention arm on sample quality? **[D]** framing\n- **C2 length** \u2014 does it degrade less as trajectory length grows far beyond the training horizon? **[D]**\n- **C3 multi-timescale** \u2014 does it preserve dynamics across timescales (spectral/autocorrelation/invariant structure), not just one-step marginals? **[D]**\n- **C-causal attribution** \u2014 is any advantage attributable to *non-causality* specifically? Gated, see \u00a76.\n\n## 2. Setup [all D/A]\n- **Model.** SiT-style diffusion/flow transformer over trajectory tokens, d=384, depth 12, ~20M params, MLP ratio 4, per-timestep tokens (or 4-step patches). Only the **temporal mixer** varies; data, tokenizer, interpolant/noise schedule, conditioning, optimizer, LR schedule, EMA, steps and loss are shared. **[D]**; the identity of \"original time attention\" (attention over timestep tokens vs. spatial/agent attention with timestep modulation) is **[A]** and is the largest interpretation risk \u2014 the design assumes temporal bidirectional attention and flags that otherwise C1\u2013C3 must be re-scoped.\n- **Lengths.** T_train = 512; evaluation grid L \u2208 {512, 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192} = {1\u00d7,2\u00d7,4\u00d7,8\u00d7,16\u00d7}. Operational \"extremely long\": **L \u2265 16\u00d7T_train with no degeneration flag and error horizon \u2265 8\u00d7T_train**. **[D]**\n- **Sampler.** Identical sampler type and step count (64) for all arms; paired noise draws across arms per test trajectory; step-count sensitivity 32/128 on the primary cell only (arms may differ in optimal steps). **[D]**\n\n### Datasets with metric-validity map (metrics used only inside their validity domain) [D]\n| Dataset | Role | Valid metrics | **Excluded** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **D1a** mixed-OU + fractional-Brownian bank (tunable power-law spectrum, stationary) | C3 mechanism test | PSD error, structure-function exponents \u03bd\u2082/\u03bd\u2084, ACF/integral-timescale error | conservation drift (no invariants); paired per-step error (stochastic) |\n| **D1c** deterministic chaotic multiscale (Lorenz-63/96 cascade, frequency-spread oscillator bank) | primary dataset for the primary endpoint | paired error growth/horizon, Lyapunov-style divergence, DMD eigenvalues, PSD (secondary) | conservation drift unless Hamiltonian variant |\n| **D2** N-body / spring-mass chain (weakly nonlinear) | conservation + long horizon | \u0394E/\u0394p drift, constraint violation, paired error horizon, time-reversal error (reversible variant) | structure functions (non-stationary) |\n| **D3** real trajectories (motion-capture joints / video tokens) | external validity only | embedding-Fr\u00e9chet, MMD, precision/recall, diversity, infill consistency | PSD/structure functions, conservation, paired error, time-reversal |\n\nD3 cannot verify dynamics, so it is a transfer check and never supports a mechanistic claim.\n\n## 3. Arms \u2014 two tiers\n**Core tier (all run).**\n- **A0** SiT + original time attention, full bidirectional [S]\n- **A1** SiT + non-causal Hyena (implicit long conv, FFT, no causal mask) [S]\n- **A2** A1 + causal mask, otherwise identical \u2014 isolates **causality** [D]\n- **A3** A0 + sliding-window attention with window = A1's kernel support at training length \u2014 isolates **receptive-field truncation**, the dominant confound since the attention arm at long L is otherwise forced to windowing [D]\n\n**Exploratory tier \u2014 explicitly declared compute-relative, ablation-only, not required for the headline claim [D]:** **A4** matched param/FLOP alternatives (TCN/short conv, linear attention) \u2014 is it \"implicit long conv + gating\" or \"any cheap mixer\"; **A5** no temporal mixer (necessity); **A6** A1 with kernel truncated to T_train (inductive bias vs kernel support); **DL** direct-long control (\u00a75) and mid-tier size bracket (\u00a77).\n\n**Matching conventions.** Primary comparison fixes **trajectory tokens + width/depth** and *reports* actual param counts. Hyena kernel params grow with kernel length (\u224818K @1024, \u2248147K @8192 for order-2, 6 heads, vs \u22480.59M per attention block), so if |\u0394params| > 5% at the operating kernel length a width-compensated Hyena arm joins the exploratory tier. FLOP-matched robustness (fewer steps for the long-trained attention arm) is secondary. **[D]**\n\n## 4. Metrics with operational definitions [D]\n**Consistency (paired ground truth: D1c, D2).** `ERR(t)` = RMSE vs. ground truth from the same initial segment. **\u03c4 is baseline-anchored, not absolute:** \u03c4 := A0's mean endpoint `ERR` at L=T_train. **`H_\u03c4`** = first t with `ERR(t) > \u03c4`; **primary scale-free score `LECS = H_\u03c4/L`** \u2208 (0,1]. `\u03b2` = OLS slope of `log ERR(t)` over the monotone window. **Infill disagreement `ID(L)`** = mean L2 gap in overlap regions when the long trajectory is generated as overlapping windows via masked denoising with shared context (works on stochastic/real data); if masking is unsupported, `ID` is dropped, not proxied. **Conservation drift** \u0394E, \u0394p (D2); **time-reversal error** (reversible variant). **Degeneration gates** (pre-hoc, symmetric): tail/data variance ratio \u2208 [0.8, 1.25]; no >2\u00d7 spectral-entropy collapse; no repeated n-gram segment > L/8 \u2014 failing an arm's cell is flagged **non-interpretable**, a validity precondition, not a second primary.\n\n**Multi-timescale (stationary only: D1a, D1c).** `D_PSD` = power-weighted \u03a3 over log-frequency bins of |log\u2081\u2080\u015c_gen \u2212 log\u2081\u2080\u015c_data|, with `D_low`/`D_high` splits (`D_low` is the specific slow-dynamics test); \u03bd\u2082, \u03bd\u2084 structure-function exponents; ACF error at decade lags + integral-timescale error; DMD/Koopman eigenvalue distance.\n\n**Quality/coverage.** Held-out trajectory-VAE latent Fr\u00e9chet, multi-bandwidth RBF-MMD, discriminative score, precision/recall@k coverage, and a diversity ratio at three horizons (quality scores alone reward collapse).\n\n**Counts.** 2048 samples per (arm \u00d7 length \u00d7 seed); 1024/4096 sensitivity on the primary cell. All thresholds/margins/counts are **[D]** arbitrary but sensitivity-tested.\n\n## 5. Length axis and the token-budget control (explicit)\nTwo regimes never mixed: **(1) extrapolation** (train 512, evaluate to 16\u00d7) and **(2) direct-long (DL)** at T=4096, separating \"extrapolates\" from \"has capacity\".\n**Same-token-budget control.** Every core arm sees an identical **1.97B trajectory tokens** at identical 60k steps with **tokens/step fixed at 32,768** (bs 64 @512 \u2192 8 @4096), and the LR schedule is defined in **tokens**, not steps, removing any implicit effective-batch confound. Stated consequence: at matched tokens the attention arm's cost grows with L (4.3 \u2192 9.7 GPU-h from T=512 \u2192 4096) while Hyena stays near-flat (4.0 \u2192 9.4), i.e. token-matching is mildly *anti*-Hyena, so a slope difference is not a data-budget artifact. Without this control the slope contrast would be confounded \u2014 hence this explicit declaration. **[D]**\n**Pre-declared fallback.** If full attention cannot run at 16\u00d7 (memory), the primary endpoint moves to the **largest length both arms support** (16\u00d7\u21928\u00d7\u21924\u00d7 grid order), fixed by the grid and not by observed results. Analytical check: fp16 attention scores \u2248 0.805 GB per layer-sample at L=8192 (6 heads; 9.66 GB summed over 12 layers uncheckpointed) \u2192 feasible with activation checkpointing and eval batch \u2264 2.\n\n## 6. Pre-registered analysis\n**Single primary endpoint:** `LECS` on **D1c** at **L = 16\u00d7T_train** for **A1**, tested for **non-inferiority against the anchor A0@T_train**, margin **\u03b4 := \u03c3\u0302(A0@T_train)** \u2014 the pooled within-arm *seed SD of the baseline at its own training length*, so the margin is variance-relative rather than a chosen number. One-sided 97.5% lower CI > \u2212\u03b4. **Power honesty:** with 6 seeds per primary cell the CI half-width is \u22481.8\u03c3\u0302 > \u03b4 = 1\u03c3\u0302, so this test can only pass if A1@16\u00d7 is at least as good as the baseline at its training length; seeds are therefore concentrated in the primary cells (6) with 3 elsewhere, and the **slope secondary carries the interpretive load**. Primary unadjusted; secondaries Holm.\n**Secondaries, pre-ordered:** S1 arm \u00d7 log(L/L_train) interaction in mixed model `LECS, D_PSD_low, ID ~ arm \u00d7 log L + (1|seed)` (C2/C3); S2 A1 vs A0 at T_train (C1); S3 `D_PSD_low`, \u03bd\u2082/\u03bd\u2084 (C3); S4 Fr\u00e9chet/MMD/coverage/diversity parity; S5 A1 vs A3 at matched receptive field; S6 **A1 vs A2**; S7 DL control; S8 D3 transfer.\n**Claim gates:** C1 \u2190 S2; **C2 \u2190 primary AND S1**; C3 \u2190 S3 with gates passed; **C-causal \u2190 S6 must survive Holm**, else the conclusion is downgraded to \"non-causal Hyena performs comparably / extrapolates better\" with no attribution to non-causality (three-valued outcome: support / downgrade / falsify). Negative control on time-reversed and shuffled-phase data must move the metrics, otherwise the metric set is declared uninformative. **Mechanistic readout** (descriptive only): learned Hyena impulse-response support vs. attention range/entropy in A0, correlated with each arm's \u03b2.\n\n## 7. Cost & feasibility (all **analytical estimates**; assumed 20 TFLOP/s effective per GPU **[A]**)\n| Item | Config | Params | Tokens | GPU-h/run | Runs | Est. GPU-h |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A0 attn, A3 win-attn | d384 z12 T512 60k bs64 | 21.5M | 1.97B | 4.3 | 6 | 25.8 |\n| A1 hyena, A2 causal hyena | d384 z12 T512 60k bs64 | 19.8M | 1.97B | 4.0 | 6 | 24.0 |\n| Primary-cell seed top-up | +3 seeds each | \u2014 | \u2014 | 4.0\u20134.3 | 6 | ~25 |\n| Eval (2048 samples \u00d7 64 steps \u00d7 5 lengths) | attn 0.05\u21922.89 h for L=512\u21928192; hyena 0.038\u21920.611 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | ~30 |\n| **Core total** | | | | | ~24 runs | **\u2248 105** |\n| DL control | attn 9.7 / hyena 9.4 (T4096, bs8, token-matched) | 21.5M | 1.97B | 9.4\u20139.7 | 4 | 38 |\n| Exploratory A4/A5/A6 | d256 z8 T512 30k bs64 | 6.4M | 0.98B | 0.7 | 6 | 4 |\n| Mid-tier transfer bracket | d768 z16 T1024 150k bs32 | ~110M | 4.92B | 53\u201357 | 2 | 110 |\n| **Grand total (all tiers)** | | | | | | **\u2248 257** |\n\n**Halved-budget pruning order (pre-declared):** (1) drop mid-tier bracket \u2192 147; (2) drop A5, A6 \u2192 143; (3) exploratory to 1 seed; (4) DL to 1 seed and T=2048 \u2192 ~120; (5) core steps 60k\u219230k and non-primary seeds 3\u21922 \u2192 **core alone \u2248 27** (train 16.9 + reduced eval). **Never pruned:** A0, A1, A2, A3 with \u22652 seeds each \u2014 losing A2/A3 would make the causality and receptive-field questions unanswerable.\n\n**Feasibility honesty.** Nothing is verified. This environment has no GPU (driver absent), no network (DNS failure) and no `torch`/`numpy`/`scipy`, so no runtime consequence of these formulas is empirically checked; every figure is closed-form arithmetic. The contemplated small CPU pilot is **only for the metric harness** (validating PSD/structure-function/MMD/conservation code against analytic ground truth such as fBm with known H and known invariants), and even that needs a dependency-provisioned environment, so it is unrun here. **No experiment was executed; no metric value, model behavior, or outcome is reported or implied.**\n\n## 8. Threats to validity\n(1) Identity of \"original time attention\" is **[A]** \u2014 if it is not temporal attention, the swap may be ill-posed. (2) Slope differences could reflect LR/step coupling at low batch \u2014 mitigated by tokens-based schedules and the DL control. (3) Attention-arm feasibility at 16\u00d7 may force the pre-declared fallback. (4) Distributional metrics can be gamed by blurring \u2014 mitigated by paired noise draws, diversity ratios, degeneration gates. (5) A non-significant A1\u2212A2 gap underpowers C-causal rather than disproving it. (6) D3 cannot support dynamics claims by construction.", "evidence": "**Cost/memory arithmetic (reproducible, run this turn):** pure-Python scripts /tmp/cost.py and /tmp/cost2.py (numpy unavailable), with training FLOPs \u2248 6\u00b7N\u00b7tokens + 12\u00b7depth\u00b7L\u00b2\u00b7d\u00b7(batch\u00b7steps) and 2\u00b7N\u00b7L (+4\u00b7depth\u00b7L\u00b2\u00b7d) per denoising step, at an assumed 20 TFLOP/s effective per GPU. Outputs quoted above: core config d=384 z=12 \u2192 21.5M (attn) / 19.8M (hyena) params, 1.97B tokens at 60k\u00d7bs64\u00d7T512, 4.3 vs 4.0 GPU-h/run; extrapolation eval per 2048 samples \u00d7 64 steps \u2014 attention 0.05/0.12/0.30/0.88/2.89 GPU-h at L=512/1024/2048/4096/8192 vs hyena 0.038/0.076/0.152/0.305/0.611 (ratio 1.3\u00d7\u21924.7\u00d7, the predicted shape of C2); token-budget-matched direct-long training with tokens/step fixed at 32768 (bs 64\u21924 as T goes 512\u21928192): atten